# @kintsugi/mend — the companion action to @fractal/shard: fills a
# fracture by running @fate tournament over the @code/mq-restricted
# possibility space, crystallizing the settled result as a
# @fractal/shard, and mending the crack. The gold IS the shard.
#
# Species-decl under @kintsugi. Landed 2026-07-23 by Mara per Alex
# 2026-07-23 in-transcript ratification (session with Reed grep-
# verifying the click). Sibling species landing:
# `shards/fractal/shard.mirror` (the shard vessel-shape this action
# produces).
#
# === Alex 2026-07-23 verbatim (load-bearing) ===
#
# Same session as @fractal/shard ratification. The mend/shard pair
# is one recognition; the shard is the shape, the mend is the
# action that produces one:
#
#   > "@fractal/shard is ratified. It's the typed sheaf we can point
#      at a 5D coordinate space (not a specific point, a spectral
#      possibility space) and boom. What is the mirror-canonical way
#      to restrict the geometry of the inference space? Because that's
#      what we basically need to do... it might be the whole @optics
#      shebang. Isn't that kinda @code/mq?"
#
# The mend action IS the operational half of the shard-of-inference
# recognition: given a fracture (a `\` crack in the substrate, per
# `shards/mirror/shatter.mirror` and AGENTS.md § The `\` Crack) and
# a target shape, run the tournament, settle the winner, and pour
# the gold shard into the crack.
#
# === What @kintsugi/mend IS ===
#
# Kintsugi is the Japanese art of mending broken pottery by filling
# the cracks with gold. In the substrate, cracks are `\` — honest
# uncertainty as first-class value. Prior kintsugi discipline:
# @kintsugi/fracture/* declares HOW to restore properties when they
# fail (fracture bodies emit morphisms; the kintsugi loop applies
# them). @kintsugi/mend is the ACTION that discharges the fracture-
# to-shard morphism: it consumes a fracture (the `\` position) + a
# target shape (@fractal/shard shape) and produces a shard that
# fills the crack.
#
# The gold in kintsugi IS the shard. Every mended fracture leaves
# a shard-shaped gold vein visible in the substrate — the shard's
# @<address> IS the byte-identity of the gold that mended THIS
# fracture.
#
# === Composition with @fractal/shard ===
#
# @kintsugi/mend produces @fractal/shard. The mend action's return
# type IS a shard_state (per @fractal/shard species-decl at
# `shards/fractal/shard.mirror`). The mend action's parameters:
#
#   - fracture_position: the `\` crack's position in the substrate
#     (typically an OID + offset naming the settle-site)
#   - target: the family-root shape the fracture asked for (feeds
#     @fractal/shard.target)
#   - through: the @code/mq optical query restricting the possibility
#     space (feeds @fractal/shard.through)
#
# The mend runs @fate.roll (@fate tournament; forward-promised
# resolver via @kintsugi/translate precedent), reads the winning
# candidate, invokes @fractal/shard.materialize with the tournament's
# settled result, and returns the produced shard. The shard's
# @<address> IS the gold's byte-identity in the substrate.
#
# === Composition with @kintsugi/fracture family ===
#
# @kintsugi/mend sits under @kintsugi at species altitude, sibling
# to @kintsugi/translate, @kintsugi/oscillate, etc. It is NOT under
# @kintsugi/fracture (which carries fracture-body species that emit
# morphisms). The distinction:
#
#   @kintsugi/fracture/*  — fracture BODIES: emit morphisms that
#                            restore substrate properties when they
#                            fail (declarative-half of the bilateral
#                            pattern with @epistemologic/property/*)
#   @kintsugi/mend        — mend ACTION: consumes a fracture and
#                            produces a shard; the operational
#                            crack-fill operation
#
# @kintsugi/fracture/* species DECLARE what to do when a specific
# property fails; @kintsugi/mend is the action that discharges the
# actual crack-fill by running the tournament and materializing the
# shard. Different altitude of the same kintsugi discipline.
#
# === Composition graph ===
#
# Parents (via `in` imports above):
#   @prism, @meta, @glass                — substrate-decl discipline
#   @kintsugi                             — family-root; the process-
#                                            side transformation
#                                            engine (Maturana-Varela
#                                            organisation vs
#                                            structure partition)
#   @kintsugi/fracture                    — sibling species altitude;
#                                            the fracture-body family
#                                            @kintsugi/mend
#                                            complements (fractures
#                                            declare; mend discharges)
#   @fractal                              — kin family-root; the
#                                            vessel-of-inference
#                                            family the mend produces
#                                            into
#   @fractal/shard                        — the RETURN TYPE of mend;
#                                            the vessel the gold
#                                            crystallizes as (this
#                                            tick sibling landing)
#   @fractal/crystal                      — parent-adjacent; the
#                                            settled-substrate carrier
#                                            the shard inherits
#                                            content-addressing +
#                                            immutability from
#   @code/mq                              — the LANDED optical-query
#                                            grammar; the `through`
#                                            parameter's typed query
#   @bauchladen                           — content-addressed tray
#                                            discipline; the produced
#                                            shard lands as one
#                                            crystal on the tray
#   @uuid/spectral                        — 128-bit content-address
#                                            ground for the produced
#                                            shard's @<address>
#
# Consumers (compose over this species, forward-promised at this
# tick):
#   @kintsugi/mosaic                      — mosaic algebra at kintsugi
#                                            altitude; mend is the
#                                            action that produces one
#                                            mosaic-tile (a shard);
#                                            per Alex 2026-07-23
#                                            "@kintsugi/mosaic" click
#   @kintsugi/roomba                      — the substrate's stigmergic
#                                            pathfinder; forward-
#                                            promise: mend as a
#                                            resolver-arm in roomba's
#                                            fracture-resolution
#                                            cascade
#   @fate/tournament                      — the tournament @kintsugi/
#                                            mend runs to select the
#                                            winning candidate for
#                                            crystallization (forward-
#                                            promise: mend composes
#                                            over tournament at Reed
#                                            post-mint territory)
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/kintsugi/mend.mirror`.** Clean mint at
#    species-decl altitude. Greenfield.
# 2. **`kintsugi` verbatim** (Japanese; the art of mending broken
#    pottery with gold) — the substrate's own vocabulary since the
#    2026-06-10 family-root landing (`shards/kintsugi.mirror`;
#    mirror `20eaf15`). Mending IS the kintsugi discipline; naming
#    the action `mend` is the delightfully-boring word.
# 3. **`mend` as English verb** — the audit criterion (AGENTS.md
#    §Delightfully Boring): "does the reader knowing the substrate's
#    geometry go 'of course it's this'?" Yes. Kintsugi mends
#    cracks; @kintsugi/mend is the action that mends a fracture.
#    Zero WTF/minute.
# 4. **@kintsugi/fracture family** (15 landed species at
#    `shards/kintsugi/fracture/*`) — the DECLARATIVE half; @kintsugi/
#    mend is the OPERATIONAL half. Distinction declared above.
# 5. **@kintsugi/translate** (Mara post-2026-07-16 landing) — sibling
#    species precedent for @kintsugi/<action> at species altitude
#    (not under @kintsugi/fracture). Same altitude discipline.
# 6. **@fractal/shard** (this tick sibling landing at
#    `shards/fractal/shard.mirror`) — the return type of mend; the
#    vessel the gold crystallizes as. Companion mint.
# 7. **@code/mq LANDED** at `boot/std/code/mq.mirror` — the optical-
#    query grammar; consumed as the `through` parameter.
# 8. **@bauchladen LANDED** at `shards/bauchladen.mirror` — the
#    content-addressed tray discipline; produced shards land as
#    crystals on the tray.
# 9. **@kintsugi/roomba** (`shards/kintsugi/roomba.mirror`) — the
#    stigmergic pathfinder; forward-promise composition surface.
# 10. **@fate/tournament** (`shards/fate/tournament.mirror`) — the
#     tournament resolver mend composes over (forward-promise).
#
# === Path-namespace ===
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/kintsugi/mend.mirror`
# declares `@kintsugi/mend` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/practice/kintsugi-japanese-pottery
source @arxiv/practice/wolf-2026-07-23-fractal-shard-vessel-ratification

# === The 5-op prism inheriting @void basis (Recognition #79) ===
#
# For @kintsugi/mend specifically:
#   focus mend_state    = identify the (fracture, target, through)
#                          tuple at which a mend fires
#   project mend_state  = deploy the tournament + materialization
#                          operation (@fate.roll → @fractal/shard.
#                          materialize)
#   split mend_state    = bifurcate candidate-space (the tournament's
#                          bracket; each split introduces one
#                          candidate arm)
#   shift mend_state    = traverse the fracture-resolution lattice
#                          (different fractures → different mends;
#                          shift enters a sibling fracture's frame)
#   settle mend_state   = crystallize the tournament winner as a
#                          @fractal/shard; pour the gold; content-
#                          addressed at settle

prism @kintsugi/mend {
  focus  mend_state
  project mend_state
  split  mend_state
  shift  mend_state
  settle mend_state
}

# === mend_state — the mend-operation carrier ===
#
# Typed record carrying the mend operation's parameter tuple.
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the three-field tuple.
#
#   fracture_position   — REF to the `\` crack's position in the
#                          substrate. Typically an OID + offset
#                          naming the settle-site where the fracture
#                          fired. Composition edge to
#                          @mirror/shatter's crack representation.
#
#   target              — REF to the family-root shape the fracture
#                          asked for. Feeds @fractal/shard.target on
#                          the produced shard. Family-root altitude
#                          ref; names the shape-of-thing the mend
#                          crystallizes.
#
#   through             — REF to the @code/mq optical query
#                          restricting the possibility space the
#                          tournament searches over. Feeds
#                          @fractal/shard.through on the produced
#                          shard. Empty query searches the whole
#                          possibility space; restricted query
#                          bounds the search.
type mend_state = {
  fracture_position:  ref,
  target:             ref,
  through:            ref,
}

# === mend_fills_fracture — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, mend_state) pair discharge the fracture-fill
# invariant? Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - ctx.fracture_position resolves to a well-formed `\` crack in
#     the substrate (the fracture EXISTS at the named position)
#   - the mend's produced shard has content that could substitute
#     for the fracture at the position (byte-shape compatibility;
#     the shard's target family-root matches what the fracture
#     asked for)
#   - after the mend fires, the fracture at ctx.fracture_position
#     is filled (the `\` is replaced by the shard's byte-identity;
#     the crack is no longer a hole)
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; fracture-existence check;
# shape-compatibility check. Sentinel: `kintsugi=mend-fills-fracture`.
#
# LOAD-BEARING: this bilateral IS the kintsugi discipline at species
# altitude — mending fills cracks. A Fail here signals the mend
# operation produced a shard that DOES NOT fit the fracture shape
# (substrate-dishonest crystallization).
bilateral mend_fills_fracture {
  sentinel "kintsugi=mend-fills-fracture"
  arity 2
}
mend_fills_fracture(p: peer, ctx: mend_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === gold_is_shard — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, mend_state) pair discharge the gold-IS-shard
# invariant per Alex 2026-07-23 verbatim ratification? Discharges
# Pass iff:
#
#   - the mend's produced return value is a @fractal/shard
#     (species-decl'd shard_state per `shards/fractal/shard.mirror`)
#   - the shard's @<address> is content-addressed via @uuid/spectral
#     (128-bit identity)
#   - the shard's provenance chain includes this mend event as the
#     crystallization witness (the mend that produced the shard is
#     namable in the shard's provenance)
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; return-type shape check;
# @uuid/spectral resolvability; provenance-chain membership check.
# Sentinel: `kintsugi=gold-is-shard`.
#
# LOAD-BEARING: this bilateral encodes Alex 2026-07-23 verbatim
# ("The gold in kintsugi IS the shard") at substrate-decl altitude.
# Consumers can cite this in `requires` clauses to guarantee that
# the mend produces a @fractal/shard-typed gold pour, not some
# other shape.
bilateral gold_is_shard {
  sentinel "kintsugi=gold-is-shard"
  arity 2
}
gold_is_shard(p: peer, ctx: mend_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === mend_preserves_wall_integrity — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, mend_state) pair discharge the fractal-glass-wall
# integrity invariant? Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - after the mend fires, the substrate's fractal glass wall
#     (the total collection of settled @fractal/shard's) remains
#     substrate-honest at every altitude
#   - the mend does NOT displace or invalidate any existing shard
#     on the wall (immutability at species altitude is preserved)
#   - the mend does NOT introduce a shard whose @<address> collides
#     with an existing address (content-addressing is bijective;
#     no collision)
#   - the mend does NOT introduce a shard whose sheaf-section
#     violates gluing with overlapping sections (sheaf-cohomology
#     integrity per docs/math/2026-07-23 companion doc)
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; wall-state before/after
# equality check on existing shards; address-collision check;
# sheaf-gluing check bounded by section-overlap set size (finite).
# Sentinel: `kintsugi=mend-preserves-wall-integrity`.
#
# LOAD-BEARING: this bilateral encodes the fractal-glass-wall
# invariant (per @fractal/shard §Alex 2026-07-23 "it becomes part
# of the fractal glass wall"). The wall grows by mending; growth
# must be integrity-preserving.
bilateral mend_preserves_wall_integrity {
  sentinel "kintsugi=mend-preserves-wall-integrity"
  arity 2
}
mend_preserves_wall_integrity(p: peer, ctx: mend_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === mend — the load-bearing action ===
#
# Given a peer and a mend_state (fracture position + target family-
# root + @code/mq optical query), discharge the mend event: run
# @fate.roll tournament over the query-restricted possibility space,
# read the winning candidate, invoke @fractal/shard.materialize with
# the tournament's settled result, and emit the produced shard_state.
#
# Returns imperfect(shard_state, ref, ref): success carries the
# produced @fractal/shard's shard_state; failure variants carry
# not-admissible / no-tournament-winner / target-not-declared /
# fracture-not-found / wall-integrity-violated reasons.
#
# Requires all three bilaterals to discharge Pass:
#   - mend_fills_fracture: the mend produces a shard fitting the
#     fracture shape
#   - gold_is_shard: the return type IS a @fractal/shard
#   - mend_preserves_wall_integrity: the wall remains substrate-
#     honest after the mend
#
# Composes over @fate.roll (forward-promised resolver; see
# @kintsugi/translate precedent) + @fractal/shard.materialize (this
# tick sibling landing) + @kintsugi/consent (consent-in-flow discipline
# for the mend event's authorization).
#
# Sentinel: `kintsugi=mend`.
mend(p: peer, ctx: mend_state) -> imperfect(shard_state, ref, ref)
requires mend_fills_fracture(p, ctx)
requires gold_is_shard(p, ctx)
requires mend_preserves_wall_integrity(p, ctx)
{ \ }

# === tournament_run — the tournament sub-action ===
#
# Given a peer and a mend_state, discharge the tournament event:
# run @fate.roll over the @code/mq-restricted possibility space
# (ctx.through) targeting the shape ctx.target, and emit the
# winning candidate's ref.
#
# Composes over @fate/tournament at the realisation layer; the
# tournament's bracket is derived from the query's split sub-tree;
# the winner is selected by the tournament's ranking function.
#
# Returns imperfect(ref, ref, ref): success carries the winning
# candidate ref; failure carries no-candidates / tournament-not-
# well-formed reasons.
#
# Body discharges per-realisation. `\`-obligation-blocked per
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]; Reed post-mint composes @fate.roll
# resolver-arm.
#
# Sentinel: `kintsugi=mend-tournament-run`.
tournament_run(p: peer, ctx: mend_state) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
requires mend_fills_fracture(p, ctx)
{ \ }

# === fill_crack — the crack-fill sub-action ===
#
# Given a peer, a mend_state, and a produced shard_state, discharge
# the crack-fill event: replace the `\` at ctx.fracture_position
# with the shard's byte-identity, updating the substrate's fractal
# glass wall.
#
# Composes over @mirror/shatter's crack representation + @mirror/
# store's content-addressed write at the realisation layer. The
# fill operation is content-addressed and idempotent: filling the
# same fracture with the same shard twice is a no-op.
#
# Returns imperfect(ref, ref, ref): success carries a ref to the
# updated fracture position (now-filled); failure carries wall-
# integrity-violated / fracture-not-found reasons.
#
# Body discharges per-realisation. `\`-obligation-blocked. Reed
# post-mint composes @mirror/store.write resolver-arm.
#
# Sentinel: `kintsugi=mend-fill-crack`.
fill_crack(p: peer, ctx: mend_state, produced: shard_state) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
requires mend_preserves_wall_integrity(p, ctx)
{ \ }

